1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,780
The next section involves the testicle,

2
00:00:01,880 --> 00:00:03,940
and the first disorder is called cryptorchidism.

3
00:00:04,400 --> 00:00:06,040
This is failure of the testicle

4
00:00:06,040 --> 00:00:07,840
to descend into the scrotal sac.

5
00:00:08,140 --> 00:00:09,660
Let's remind ourselves embryologically

6
00:00:09,660 --> 00:00:12,060
that the testicle normally develops in the abdomen,

7
00:00:12,480 --> 00:00:14,380
and then it descends into the scrotal sac

8
00:00:14,380 --> 00:00:15,460
as the fetus grows.

9
00:00:15,900 --> 00:00:18,700
If it fails to descend, that's called cryptorchidism.

10
00:00:19,120 --> 00:00:20,900
This is the most common congenital male

11
00:00:20,900 --> 00:00:22,720
reproductive abnormality.

12
00:00:23,120 --> 00:00:25,860
It's seen in about 1% of male infants.

13
00:00:26,340 --> 00:00:27,820
Now what I should remind you of is that

14
00:00:27,820 --> 00:00:29,680
most cases would actually resolve

15
00:00:29,680 --> 00:00:30,640
spontaneously.

16
00:00:31,320 --> 00:00:33,500
However, if it doesn't resolve by the age of 2,

17
00:00:33,780 --> 00:00:35,580
then the surgeon would go in and actually

18
00:00:35,580 --> 00:00:38,500
perform a procedure called orcapexy,

19
00:00:38,500 --> 00:00:41,140
where they tack the testicle down into the scrotal sac,

20
00:00:41,440 --> 00:00:43,540
and that's because after the age of 2,

21
00:00:43,620 --> 00:00:46,200
you can begin to get damage to the germ cells,

22
00:00:46,520 --> 00:00:48,260
and that plays into the complication,

23
00:00:48,420 --> 00:00:49,820
which is that there's an increased risk

24
00:00:49,820 --> 00:00:52,180
for testicular atrophy with infertility,

25
00:00:52,660 --> 00:00:54,580
and that's because the testicle normally

26
00:00:54,580 --> 00:00:55,900
needs to be at a lower temperature,

27
00:00:56,020 --> 00:00:57,840
and if it's up high in the body,

28
00:00:57,980 --> 00:00:59,440
it won't be at that low temperature.

29
00:00:59,440 --> 00:01:01,260
The purpose of keeping the testicle

30
00:01:01,260 --> 00:01:03,380
and the scrotal sac is to keep the temperature low,

31
00:01:03,660 --> 00:01:05,400
which is a little lower than the body temperature.

32
00:01:05,900 --> 00:01:07,960
So there'd be an increased risk for testicular atrophy

33
00:01:07,960 --> 00:01:11,200
with infertility if you let it go beyond the age of 2,

34
00:01:11,380 --> 00:01:13,260
and also there's an increased risk for development

35
00:01:13,260 --> 00:01:15,140
of a germ cell tumor called seminoma,

36
00:01:15,560 --> 00:01:17,720
and so basically if these patients don't resolve

37
00:01:17,720 --> 00:01:20,300
by the age of 2, they're going to get orcapexy.

38
00:01:21,260 --> 00:01:23,320
Orchitis refers to inflammation of the testicle.

39
00:01:23,640 --> 00:01:25,480
It can classically be seen with chlamydia,

40
00:01:25,480 --> 00:01:28,780
so chlamydia trachomatis, in particular serotypes D through K,

41
00:01:28,860 --> 00:01:32,600
can lead to orchitis, it's again sexually transmitted disease.

42
00:01:33,000 --> 00:01:34,880
Neisseria gonorrhea can also do it.

43
00:01:35,220 --> 00:01:38,140
E. coli and pseudomonas would be seen in older adults.

44
00:01:38,300 --> 00:01:41,140
Basically, these are the urinary tract infection bugs

45
00:01:41,140 --> 00:01:43,100
that would normally be seen in older adults,

46
00:01:43,420 --> 00:01:45,840
and so they can also spread into the reproductive tract.

47
00:01:46,620 --> 00:01:48,140
And so basically when you think about orchitis,

48
00:01:48,220 --> 00:01:50,740
you think about chlamydia trachomatis, D through K,

49
00:01:50,740 --> 00:01:54,280
and Neisseria in younger sexually active adults,

50
00:01:54,720 --> 00:01:58,300
and then E. coli and pseudomonas in older adults.

51
00:01:58,960 --> 00:02:00,560
Mumps virus can also do it.

52
00:02:00,640 --> 00:02:01,940
Remember that when we talked about mumps,

53
00:02:02,000 --> 00:02:05,960
we mentioned that mumps classically inflames the parotid glands.

54
00:02:06,280 --> 00:02:08,400
However, it can also inflame three other tissues.

55
00:02:08,820 --> 00:02:10,380
You can get infection within the meninges,

56
00:02:10,440 --> 00:02:11,820
giving you an aseptic meningitis.

57
00:02:12,200 --> 00:02:13,720
You can get pancreatitis,

58
00:02:14,040 --> 00:02:16,180
and then finally you can get orchitis.

59
00:02:16,180 --> 00:02:17,800
And so if there's orchitis,

60
00:02:17,900 --> 00:02:21,160
there would be a increased risk for infertility.

61
00:02:21,480 --> 00:02:23,400
But remember that orchitis is not usually seen

62
00:02:23,400 --> 00:02:25,460
until the patients are greater than the age of 10.

63
00:02:25,960 --> 00:02:28,340
And finally, you can get something called autoimmune orchitis,

64
00:02:28,420 --> 00:02:31,440
in which there's autoimmune destruction of the testicular tissue.

65
00:02:31,840 --> 00:02:33,460
And the classic hallmark of this

66
00:02:33,460 --> 00:02:36,680
is that you get granulomas that involve the tubules of the testicle.

67
00:02:37,120 --> 00:02:39,660
So granulomatous inflammation of the testicle,

68
00:02:39,860 --> 00:02:40,880
you think about two things.

69
00:02:40,920 --> 00:02:41,640
You think about TB,

70
00:02:42,200 --> 00:02:43,620
and you think about autoimmune orchitis.

71
00:02:43,620 --> 00:02:46,920
And of course, you can prove TB by doing an AFB stain

72
00:02:46,920 --> 00:02:49,580
and trying to find the acid fast bacilli

73
00:02:49,580 --> 00:02:51,100
that would be indicative of TB.

74
00:02:51,480 --> 00:02:52,220
And also in TB,

75
00:02:52,340 --> 00:02:54,620
you often would see necrotizing granulomas,

76
00:02:54,900 --> 00:02:56,680
whereas in autoimmune orchitis,

77
00:02:56,780 --> 00:02:58,600
the granulomas would be non-necrotizing.

78
00:02:59,840 --> 00:03:01,460
Testicular torsion occurs

79
00:03:01,460 --> 00:03:03,180
when you have twisting of the spermatic cord,

80
00:03:03,440 --> 00:03:05,820
which then leads to hemorrhagic infarction of the testicle.

81
00:03:06,280 --> 00:03:07,540
It's a very simple principle.

82
00:03:07,760 --> 00:03:08,960
You've got the spermatic cord,

83
00:03:09,020 --> 00:03:11,920
and there's obviously blood artery and vein going in and out.

84
00:03:11,920 --> 00:03:14,280
And then you've got the testicle hanging on that cord.

85
00:03:14,660 --> 00:03:17,000
If you twist the testicle around that cord,

86
00:03:17,320 --> 00:03:20,760
you are going to close off the thin-walled vein,

87
00:03:21,140 --> 00:03:23,560
but the thick-walled artery will remain open.

88
00:03:23,980 --> 00:03:26,680
And so blood will come in, but blood can't go out.

89
00:03:26,940 --> 00:03:28,840
And if blood comes in but can't go out,

90
00:03:29,160 --> 00:03:30,900
that's going to eventually lead to infarction.

91
00:03:31,460 --> 00:03:33,200
And so in this particular case,

92
00:03:33,260 --> 00:03:34,500
they get a hemorrhagic infarction

93
00:03:34,500 --> 00:03:35,840
because blood keeps going in,

94
00:03:35,900 --> 00:03:37,740
but you're not going to get flow across the organ

95
00:03:37,740 --> 00:03:40,080
because you blocked the venous drainage.

96
00:03:40,520 --> 00:03:42,560
So that lack of blood flow across the organ

97
00:03:42,560 --> 00:03:43,820
will then result in infarction.

98
00:03:44,180 --> 00:03:45,300
And of course, it would be hemorrhagic

99
00:03:45,300 --> 00:03:46,800
because blood is still coming in

100
00:03:46,800 --> 00:03:49,120
and because this is a loosely organized tissue.

101
00:03:49,560 --> 00:03:51,140
Remember that to get hemorrhagic infarction,

102
00:03:51,280 --> 00:03:51,920
you need two things.

103
00:03:51,980 --> 00:03:53,700
You need blood going into the space

104
00:03:53,700 --> 00:03:55,020
after the tissue has died,

105
00:03:55,440 --> 00:03:57,280
plus you need a loosely organized tissue.

106
00:03:57,840 --> 00:03:59,820
So that's what I say here about testicular infarction.

107
00:03:59,900 --> 00:04:01,720
It occurs with twisting of the spermatic cord,

108
00:04:01,780 --> 00:04:03,480
which leads to hemorrhagic infarction.

109
00:04:03,480 --> 00:04:07,000
It can be due to congenital failure of the testes

110
00:04:07,000 --> 00:04:09,200
to attach to the inner lining of the scrotum.

111
00:04:09,560 --> 00:04:11,140
Now remember that the testes at their base

112
00:04:11,140 --> 00:04:13,380
are normally attached to the inner lining of the scrotum.

113
00:04:13,720 --> 00:04:14,700
And so if they're not attached,

114
00:04:14,840 --> 00:04:16,760
then you can easily get a twisting

115
00:04:16,760 --> 00:04:18,580
of the testicle on that cord.

116
00:04:19,080 --> 00:04:20,880
The classically presents an adolescence

117
00:04:20,880 --> 00:04:23,620
and it presents with sudden testicular pain

118
00:04:23,620 --> 00:04:25,560
and an absent cremasteric reflux.

119
00:04:26,140 --> 00:04:27,740
The cremasteric reflux is

120
00:04:27,740 --> 00:04:29,340
when you take a tongue depressor

121
00:04:29,340 --> 00:04:32,440
and scrape it along the inner aspect of the thigh.

122
00:04:32,440 --> 00:04:34,220
That would cause the scrotum,

123
00:04:34,440 --> 00:04:37,040
the muscles of the scrotum to actually contract

124
00:04:37,040 --> 00:04:38,880
and it would draw the scrotum upward.

125
00:04:39,520 --> 00:04:40,720
And so in this particular case,

126
00:04:40,800 --> 00:04:43,600
because the nerves that are necessary

127
00:04:43,600 --> 00:04:45,000
for that cremasteric reflux

128
00:04:45,000 --> 00:04:47,120
are also coming through the cord,

129
00:04:47,460 --> 00:04:48,480
in this particular case,

130
00:04:48,540 --> 00:04:49,560
when the tissue is dead

131
00:04:49,560 --> 00:04:53,820
and you tried to scrape with a tongue depressor

132
00:04:53,820 --> 00:04:54,960
along the inner thigh,

133
00:04:55,160 --> 00:04:57,180
you wouldn't get that cremasteric reflux.

134
00:04:57,260 --> 00:04:59,140
And that's an important clinical finding.

135
00:04:59,240 --> 00:05:01,000
And again, it's high yield for exams as well.

136
00:05:01,000 --> 00:05:03,740
Here's a picture of a testicular torsion

137
00:05:03,740 --> 00:05:05,500
with a hemorrhagic infarction of the testicle.

138
00:05:05,600 --> 00:05:06,640
You can see that the testicle

139
00:05:06,640 --> 00:05:09,380
has basically been reduced to a sack of blood.

140
00:05:10,700 --> 00:05:12,200
A varicocele is when you have dilation

141
00:05:12,200 --> 00:05:15,020
of the spermatic vein due to impaired drainage.

142
00:05:15,460 --> 00:05:17,700
And that's gonna present a scrotal swelling

143
00:05:17,700 --> 00:05:19,460
with a bag of worms appearance.

144
00:05:19,740 --> 00:05:21,220
Now, the idea here is that

145
00:05:21,220 --> 00:05:23,240
all of the veins become dilated

146
00:05:23,240 --> 00:05:25,400
and you see them on the surface of the scrotum.

147
00:05:25,460 --> 00:05:26,180
That's the key thing.

148
00:05:26,460 --> 00:05:27,960
And so it looks like a bag of worms

149
00:05:27,960 --> 00:05:28,800
and you can feel it

150
00:05:28,800 --> 00:05:30,440
and it also feels like a bag of worms.

151
00:05:30,980 --> 00:05:32,660
Varicoceles are usually left-sided

152
00:05:32,660 --> 00:05:33,580
and they're associated

153
00:05:33,580 --> 00:05:35,640
with left-sided renal cell carcinoma as well.

154
00:05:35,940 --> 00:05:37,280
This is particularly high yield

155
00:05:37,280 --> 00:05:38,520
because it goes back to anatomy.

156
00:05:38,880 --> 00:05:39,880
So I just wanna take a moment

157
00:05:39,880 --> 00:05:41,840
to draw what's going on on the left side.

158
00:05:42,220 --> 00:05:43,340
Let's go back to the whiteboard.

159
00:05:43,440 --> 00:05:44,700
Here's the inferior vena cava

160
00:05:44,700 --> 00:05:46,940
and you've got the renal vein coming in

161
00:05:46,940 --> 00:05:48,280
to the inferior vena cava.

162
00:05:48,700 --> 00:05:51,040
So this is again the inferior vena cava.

163
00:05:51,520 --> 00:05:52,780
Now the idea here is that

164
00:05:52,780 --> 00:05:54,580
when you look at the spermatic vein

165
00:05:54,580 --> 00:05:55,980
on the left side,

166
00:05:56,220 --> 00:05:58,740
the spermatic vein goes into the renal vein

167
00:05:58,740 --> 00:06:00,100
and then eventually the renal vein

168
00:06:00,100 --> 00:06:02,060
then drains into the inferior vena cava.

169
00:06:02,500 --> 00:06:04,520
And so this creates an extra step

170
00:06:04,520 --> 00:06:05,320
for that drainage

171
00:06:05,320 --> 00:06:07,320
and therefore because there's an extra step,

172
00:06:07,440 --> 00:06:08,340
there's an increased risk

173
00:06:08,340 --> 00:06:12,360
for developing varicoceles on the left side.

174
00:06:12,620 --> 00:06:13,800
Whereas on the opposite side,

175
00:06:13,860 --> 00:06:15,340
if this were the right side, for example,

176
00:06:15,660 --> 00:06:16,660
this is the renal vein,

177
00:06:16,900 --> 00:06:18,340
the spermatic vein goes directly

178
00:06:18,340 --> 00:06:19,540
into the inferior vena cava

179
00:06:19,540 --> 00:06:21,580
so it doesn't have to go through that extra space.

180
00:06:21,580 --> 00:06:24,480
And so it's less likely to develop varicoceles

181
00:06:24,480 --> 00:06:25,780
on that right side.

182
00:06:26,080 --> 00:06:26,860
Now at the same time,

183
00:06:26,920 --> 00:06:28,860
let's say that a patient has a renal cell carcinoma.

184
00:06:29,100 --> 00:06:30,260
You're well aware of the fact

185
00:06:30,260 --> 00:06:32,820
that renal cell carcinoma loves to invade the renal vein.

186
00:06:33,180 --> 00:06:34,140
It's one of the carcinomas

187
00:06:34,140 --> 00:06:35,460
that likes to go into the vein.

188
00:06:35,880 --> 00:06:37,320
And so when renal cell carcinoma

189
00:06:37,320 --> 00:06:38,580
goes into the renal vein,

190
00:06:38,960 --> 00:06:40,500
we're gonna get blocking of the renal vein

191
00:06:40,500 --> 00:06:42,420
which would block the drainage of the spermatic vein

192
00:06:42,420 --> 00:06:44,440
and therefore give you a varicocele

193
00:06:44,440 --> 00:06:46,500
in particular on the left side.

194
00:06:46,940 --> 00:06:48,140
So this is super high yield.

195
00:06:48,220 --> 00:06:49,560
It shows up on exams all the time.

196
00:06:49,660 --> 00:06:51,360
The varicoceles are usually left-sided

197
00:06:51,360 --> 00:06:52,580
and they're associated

198
00:06:52,580 --> 00:06:54,380
with left-sided renal cell carcinoma.

199
00:06:55,240 --> 00:06:56,580
Also, varicoceles can be seen

200
00:06:56,580 --> 00:06:58,540
in a large percentage of infertile males.

201
00:06:59,040 --> 00:07:00,100
And the idea here,

202
00:07:00,180 --> 00:07:01,100
one of the theories here

203
00:07:01,100 --> 00:07:02,300
is that if you've got a varicocele,

204
00:07:02,360 --> 00:07:04,340
you've got a lot of warm blood piling up

205
00:07:04,340 --> 00:07:05,800
in the scrotal sac.

206
00:07:06,080 --> 00:07:08,000
And if you've got a lot of warm blood piling up,

207
00:07:08,060 --> 00:07:09,560
that potentially is going to warm

208
00:07:09,560 --> 00:07:11,760
the temperature of the overall testicle

209
00:07:11,760 --> 00:07:13,680
which would then result in infertility.

210
00:07:13,920 --> 00:07:14,880
That hasn't been proven,

211
00:07:15,020 --> 00:07:16,280
but anyway, it's one theory

212
00:07:16,280 --> 00:07:17,940
of why there's this association.

213
00:07:18,900 --> 00:07:20,840
A hydrocele is when you have fluid collection

214
00:07:20,840 --> 00:07:22,300
within the tunica vaginalis.

215
00:07:22,500 --> 00:07:23,900
Let's pretend this is the testicle.

216
00:07:24,000 --> 00:07:26,460
Remember that there is a layer of cirrhosa

217
00:07:26,460 --> 00:07:27,540
that's on the testicle

218
00:07:27,540 --> 00:07:28,660
and it sort of comes around

219
00:07:28,660 --> 00:07:32,140
and also attaches to the scrotal skin out here.

220
00:07:32,620 --> 00:07:34,660
And so this is called the tunica vaginalis.

221
00:07:34,740 --> 00:07:36,800
Now, it normally has a minimal amount of fluid

222
00:07:36,800 --> 00:07:38,680
and it's really imperceptible.

223
00:07:39,060 --> 00:07:40,880
However, when you fill this with fluid,

224
00:07:41,160 --> 00:07:42,200
as you fill it with fluid,

225
00:07:42,300 --> 00:07:43,920
that's going to result in fluid building

226
00:07:43,920 --> 00:07:45,080
in the scrotal sac,

227
00:07:45,420 --> 00:07:47,180
and that's called a hydrosele.

228
00:07:47,180 --> 00:07:49,560
Now, it's associated with incomplete closure

229
00:07:49,560 --> 00:07:51,600
of the process vaginalis in infants.

230
00:07:52,220 --> 00:07:54,020
Now, remember that when you form the scrotum,

231
00:07:54,160 --> 00:07:56,800
it actually is an invagination of the peritoneum

232
00:07:57,380 --> 00:07:58,640
that comes down like this

233
00:07:58,640 --> 00:08:01,800
to form the tunica vaginalis.

234
00:08:01,840 --> 00:08:05,200
So if this is not sealed properly up here,

235
00:08:05,460 --> 00:08:07,640
then you can have a connection with the peritoneum

236
00:08:07,640 --> 00:08:10,220
which then could provide fluid to this region

237
00:08:10,220 --> 00:08:12,480
and that's what you would see in infants.

238
00:08:12,640 --> 00:08:14,280
A failure, and this again is a failure

239
00:08:14,280 --> 00:08:16,540
of the closure of the process vaginalis.

240
00:08:16,960 --> 00:08:19,240
At the same time, it's possible to see it in adults

241
00:08:19,240 --> 00:08:20,620
and if you see it in adults,

242
00:08:20,720 --> 00:08:24,480
it's due to blockage of lymphatic drainage classically.

243
00:08:24,960 --> 00:08:26,660
Now, this presents a scrotal swelling

244
00:08:26,660 --> 00:08:28,340
and it can be transluminated

245
00:08:28,340 --> 00:08:29,640
which means that if you took light

246
00:08:29,640 --> 00:08:31,320
and you shined it across the scrotum,

247
00:08:31,600 --> 00:08:32,940
you would be able to get light through there

248
00:08:32,940 --> 00:08:34,660
and that's because you don't have a solid mass,

249
00:08:34,720 --> 00:08:35,860
you just have a bag of fluid.

250
00:08:36,240 --> 00:08:37,620
This is what the hydroseal looks like.

251
00:08:37,620 --> 00:08:39,720
You just have a swollen scrotum

252
00:08:39,720 --> 00:08:41,420
and that's because it's loaded with fluid.

253
00:08:41,940 --> 00:08:43,240
And that concludes this section.

254
00:08:43,240 --> 00:08:44,240
Thank you.

255
00:08:44,240 --> 00:08:45,240
Thank you.

